.cache/
*.lock
*.corrupted.*

# Install-local snapshots — `fabric install` always-rewrites these, and their
# contents are about THIS machine (absolute target path, scan timestamp, the
# digests of the copies this install wrote). Tracking them means every install
# dirties the tree, and a teammate's `install_copy_drift` baseline would be
# whoever committed last rather than their own install. Absent on a fresh
# clone is the correct state — doctor says "run `fabric install`" and does.
forensic.json
install-manifest.json
